my name is mandana i'm from iran  and i  am born in tehran and i grew up there  i lived there for 22 years and then i  moved to montreal  my research is about the role of memory  in reinforcement learning  and how that can improve the  computational efficiency of algorithms  basically i study how a memory mechanism  in human can advance rl algorithms  to solve real-world problems  so more specifically i study  representation and abstraction learned  by these models  and i work on a principal approach to  learn how we can improve the  computational efficiency of  reinforcement algorithms  by getting inspiration from human memory  it's not really a single person  and  it changes through time depending on a  project that i'm working on  um  but  yeah there are a lot of people who i try  to follow their works it's not just one  person  [Music]  i first did an internship at mila and  i spent almost six months here  and then i started to know the people  the student life at mila and i realized  that the research interests of a lot of  people here are  greatly aligned with mine and that was a  great motivation for me to start my phd  right after  and also i really like montreal so i'm  living here for almost five years  and i think it's a great city for  students if they want to spend their  time and just meet new people  and it has a great multicultural living  environment that i quite appreciate  enjoy the learning process  as much as the outcome so  don't just try to make great results  even though that is that's perfect but  also try to  learn  as much as you can when you are making  progress and i'd say the journey matters  as much as the destination  [Music]
 

